You are implementing Task 1.2: Configure Design System

## Task Description

Set up the complete design system for Vibe Voyager — a space-themed game with clean minimalist sci-fi aesthetics (glassmorphism, parallax, SVG planets).

### Step 1: Set up Tailwind v4 theme in globals.css

Replace the contents of `app/globals.css` with the design tokens. Tailwind v4 uses CSS-first config — no tailwind.config.js needed.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --color-void: #0a0f1a;
  --color-void-light: #111827;
  --color-nebula: #4a6fa5;
  --color-nebula-light: #5d85bf;
  --color-nebula-dark: #3a5a8a;
  --color-signal: #6b9e78;
  --color-signal-light: #7fb88d;
  --color-signal-dark: #5a8766;
  --color-terracotta: #c17147;
  --color-terracotta-light: #d4855c;
  --color-terracotta-dark: #a85e3a;
  --color-starlight: #e8e0d4;
  --color-starlight-dim: #b8b0a4;
  --color-glass: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  --color-glass-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  --color-glass-hover: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  --color-glass-active: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);

  --font-display: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-body: "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;

  --shadow-glow-nebula: 0 0 20px rgba(74, 111, 165, 0.3);
  --shadow-glow-signal: 0 0 20px rgba(107, 158, 120, 0.3);
  --shadow-glow-terracotta: 0 0 20px rgba(193, 113, 71, 0.3);
  --shadow-glow-starlight: 0 0 20px rgba(232, 224, 212, 0.2);
}

/* Base styles */
body {
  background-color: var(--color-void);
  color: var(--color-starlight);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
}

/* Smooth scrolling */
html {
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

/* Selection color */
::selection {
  background-color: rgba(74, 111, 165, 0.3);
  color: var(--color-starlight);
}

/* Custom scrollbar */
::-webkit-scrollbar {
  width: 6px;
}
::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
  background: var(--color-void);
}
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: var(--color-glass-border);
  border-radius: 3px;
}
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
  background: var(--color-glass-hover);
}
```

### Step 2: Configure layout.tsx with Google Fonts

Replace `app/layout.tsx` with:

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next'
import { Space_Grotesk, Inter, JetBrains_Mono } from 'next/font/google'
import './globals.css'

const spaceGrotesk = Space_Grotesk({
  variable: '--font-display',
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap',
})

const inter = Inter({
  variable: '--font-body',
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap',
})

const jetbrainsMono = JetBrains_Mono({
  variable: '--font-mono',
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap',
})

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Vibe Voyager — The Agentic Coding Odyssey',
  description: 'An interactive space exploration game teaching vibe coding, agentic AI, and modern software engineering. From beginner to agentic developer.',
  keywords: ['vibe coding', 'agentic AI', 'AI engineering', 'MCP', 'Claude Code', 'interactive learning'],
  authors: [{ name: 'Shehral' }],
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Vibe Voyager — The Agentic Coding Odyssey',
    description: 'An interactive space exploration game teaching vibe coding, agentic AI, and modern software engineering.',
    type: 'website',
    url: 'https://[REDACTED_DOMAIN]',
  },
}

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: Readonly<{
  children: React.ReactNode
}>) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={`${spaceGrotesk.variable} ${inter.variable} ${jetbrainsMono.variable}`}>
      <body className="bg-void text-starlight font-body antialiased min-h-screen overflow-x-hidden">
        {children}
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

### Step 3: Create shared constants

Create `lib/constants.ts`:

```typescript
export const COLORS = {
  void: '#0a0f1a',
  nebula: '#4a6fa5',
  signal: '#6b9e78',
  terracotta: '#c17147',
  starlight: '#e8e0d4',
} as const

export const RANKS = [
  { name: 'Cadet', min: 4, max: 10 },
  { name: 'Navigator', min: 11, max: 20 },
  { name: 'Commander', min: 21, max: 30 },
  { name: 'Admiral', min: 31, max: 40 },
] as const

export const STATS = ['vibe', 'architecture', 'protocol', 'command'] as const
export type StatName = (typeof STATS)[number]

export const STAT_COLORS: Record<StatName, string> = {
  vibe: '#c17147',
  architecture: '#4a6fa5',
  protocol: '#6b9e78',
  command: '#e8e0d4',
}

export const STAT_LABELS: Record<StatName, string> = {
  vibe: 'Vibe',
  architecture: 'Architecture',
  protocol: 'Protocol',
  command: 'Command',
}
```

### Step 4: Create a simple test page to verify the design system works

Replace `app/page.tsx` with a temporary test page that demonstrates the design system:

```tsx
export default function Home() {
  return (
    <main className="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center">
      <div className="text-center space-y-8">
        <h1 className="font-display text-6xl tracking-wider text-starlight">
          VIBE VOYAGER
        </h1>
        <p className="font-body text-xl text-starlight-dim">
          The Agentic Coding Odyssey
        </p>
        <div className="flex gap-4 justify-center">
          <div className="px-6 py-3 bg-glass border border-glass-border rounded-xl backdrop-blur-md text-nebula">
            Glassmorphism Panel
          </div>
          <div className="px-6 py-3 bg-glass border border-glass-border rounded-xl backdrop-blur-md text-signal">
            Signal Green
          </div>
          <div className="px-6 py-3 bg-glass border border-glass-border rounded-xl backdrop-blur-md text-terracotta">
            Terracotta
          </div>
        </div>
        <p className="font-mono text-sm text-starlight-dim">
          const agent = await createAgent(config)
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>
  )
}
```

### Step 5: Verify and commit

Run `npm run dev`, verify:
- Page loads with dark (#0a0f1a) background
- Title "VIBE VOYAGER" renders in Space Grotesk
- Body text in Inter
- Code text in JetBrains Mono
- Glassmorphism panels visible with correct colors
- Kill dev server after verifying

Commit:
```bash
git add app/globals.css app/layout.tsx app/page.tsx lib/constants.ts
git commit -m "feat: configure Tailwind v4 design system with color tokens and typography

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
```

## Context

This is Phase 1.2 of the Vibe Voyager implementation. Phase 1.1 (project scaffolding) is complete. This design system defines the visual language used by ALL subsequent components — every GlassPanel, StatGauge, button, and page will reference these tokens. Getting this right means every future agent produces consistent visuals.

## Your Job

1. Implement exactly what's described above
2. Verify the dev server shows correct fonts and colors
3. Commit your work
4. Report back

